📊 Week 7: Visualization & Dashboard Development

In Week 7, the focus was on building effective visualizations and dashboards to present insights derived from the IT Support dataset. This phase emphasized transforming analytical results into clear, interactive, and visually appealing representations for better understanding and decision-making.

Multiple visualization techniques were implemented using tools such as Matplotlib, Seaborn, Plotly, and Microsoft Power BI. These tools were used to create both static and interactive charts.

Different types of visualizations were developed to analyze key aspects of the dataset:

Bar charts to represent ticket distribution across categories and countries
Line charts to analyze trends in resolution time and ticket volume over time
Heatmaps to identify patterns and performance variations across priorities and regions
Geographical maps to visualize country-wise ticket trends and performance

The dashboard also included insights such as:

Ticket distribution by category and country
Resolution efficiency based on priority levels
Cluster performance compared with similarity scores
Regional trends and performance differences

The visualizations were designed to be interactive, allowing users to explore data dynamically and gain deeper insights. This enhances the ability to monitor performance, identify patterns, and support data-driven decision-making.

Overall, Week 7 focused on presenting data in a meaningful and visually intuitive way, making complex insights easier to understand and actionable for improving IT support performance.
